-- title:
--   At new places of a constant field extension, dx has order 0
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $F$, $K'$, $F'$ be fields with $F/K$ and $F'/K'$ algebras, together with $K$-algebra maps $K\to K'$, $F\to F'$ and $K\to F'$ forming compatible scalar towers ($K\to K'\to F'$ and $K\to F\to F'$), and let $K$ have characteristic $0$. Assume: there is $x_0\in F$ transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over $K(x_0)$, and likewise some $x_0'\in F'$ transcendental over $K'$ with $F'$ finite-dimensional over $K'(x_0')$; that $F'$ is a curve over $K'$ in the project's sense, i.e. every nonzero $f\in F'$ admits a divisor of degree $0$ whose value at each place is $\operatorname{ord}_v f$, every place of $F'/K'$ has residue field finite over $K'$, and $\Omega_{F'/K'}$ is free of rank one over $F'$; and that the $K'$-subextension of $F'$ generated by the image of $F$ is all of $F'$. Let $w$ be a place of $F'/K'$, that is a valuation subring of $F'$ containing the image of $K'$, not equal to $F'$, and a principal ideal ring, and suppose the image of every $f\in F$ lies in that valuation subring. Let $x\in F$ be such that its image in $F'$ is transcendental over $K'$. Then, writing $\mathrm{d}x$ for $\mathrm{D}_{K'}(F')$ applied to the image of $x$, the coefficient of $\mathrm{d}x$ with respect to the differential $\mathrm{d}\pi_w$ of the chosen uniformiser at $w$ — the element $c\in F'$ selected when $\mathrm{d}x = c\cdot \mathrm{d}\pi_w$ is solvable, and $0$ otherwise — is nonzero and satisfies $\operatorname{ord}_w(c)=0$.
--
--   This is the statement that the places of a constant field extension $F'=FK'$ which lie over no place of $F$ (those whose valuation ring swallows all of $F$) contribute nothing to the canonical degree: at such a place the differential of a function coming from $F$ has neither zero nor pole. It is used, alongside the unramified lifting of the old places, in the proof that the genus is unchanged under extension of an algebraically closed constant field ([`AlgebraicCurve.genus_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.genus_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed)).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_ordDifferential_D_eq_zero_of_constantFieldExtension_of_forall_mem.lean

